{"id": "EUVD-2026-103916", "enisaUuid": "c89e5540-355b-342e-ad15-56aecab96fc3", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: light: gp2ap020a00f: drain irq_work after free_irq\n\nThe threaded IRQ handler queues data->work through irq_work_queue() so\nthe trigger is polled from a per-CPU context.  free_irq() does not flush\nan irq_work the handler already queued, so after gp2ap020a00f_remove()\nreturns that work may still run and call iio_trigger_poll() on data->trig,\nwhich the devm cleanup has already freed, causing a use-after-free.\n\nAdd irq_work_sync(&data->work) after free_irq() in remove() and in the\nprobe error path, mirroring commit 78601726d4a5 (\"iio: trigger: sysfs:\nfix use-after-free on remove\").\n\nFound by an in-house static analysis tool, confirmed by manual review.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:44:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:27", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/85c20d1cf3f01a506605a16c2f9ce23b9c8b114f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a36814b9fe00970116d30c3143d81e7425c4d334", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cc71400bc965c0d3894a38ead3d71243400c2d5e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a1769877ff52a4f1bfb9ca535d1b5113808bd602", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/63213927b141085b6c8719b8037dab3074b7e0fe"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98662", "GHSA-5vf6-9cv6-xwcm"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b843e3f-ef16-314a-bbd4-0712d6b79a7a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "4d95c064-72b9-3d3b-90d2-1baad45be55e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bf29fbeaa13d3350ca71df70c705d8b883c45692 <a1769877ff52a4f1bfb9ca535d1b5113808bd602"}, {"id": "50d3f3c9-9373-3035-9ccd-6b6bea760e49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "640f3f04-1d15-33ae-b2f3-f44627fbf20c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bf29fbeaa13d3350ca71df70c705d8b883c45692 <cc71400bc965c0d3894a38ead3d71243400c2d5e"}, {"id": "75e45672-d867-385f-ba1e-b093e9f92bd3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "78582bcd-30a2-3932-8364-da4e8d49e6c9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bf29fbeaa13d3350ca71df70c705d8b883c45692 <85c20d1cf3f01a506605a16c2f9ce23b9c8b114f"}, {"id": "b9f76be1-d42a-34d6-a207-eedff3c5684c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bf29fbeaa13d3350ca71df70c705d8b883c45692 <a36814b9fe00970116d30c3143d81e7425c4d334"}, {"id": "c7a7db80-f790-35e7-bf1f-cd8795dc67f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d9ad435b-24d2-3f65-a464-50c623a0dd2a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "e67caa49-6c1e-30d8-8cfa-50957cad5acc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "eb20bc9a-6b5b-34b6-bd62-d6af8a064ae9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bf29fbeaa13d3350ca71df70c705d8b883c45692 <63213927b141085b6c8719b8037dab3074b7e0fe"}, {"id": "feaec220-e8c8-3f8e-9eba-f12dbc076a73", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.13"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "db452f37-1e7a-3ac0-9ca0-3724a13536d6", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}